  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{P}(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma)$ be the image of the point $\\mathrm{Q}(3,-3,1)$ in the line $\\frac{x-0}{1}=\\frac{y-3}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}$ and $\\mathrm{R}$ be the point $(2,5,-1)$. If the area of the triangle $P Q R$ is $\\lambda$ and $\\lambda^2=14 K$, then $K$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "36",
      "is_correct": false
    },
